         "align": "left",
         "shade": null,
         "borders": null,
         "marker": null
        },
        "content": [
         {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "-    Tinea versicolor, extensive + recurrent: oral antifungals (pts prefer for convenience, but more AEs — liver damage, harmful drug interactions → use sparingly); fluconazole = safest oral agent, weekly x2–4 wk; once every 6 mo if high risk of recurrence"
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
         "indLeft": 36,
         "indRight": 0,
         "indFirst": -18,
         "spaceBefore": 0,
         "spaceAfter": 0,
         "line": {
          "rule": "auto",
          "value": 1
         },
         "align": "left",
         "shade": null,
         "borders": null,
         "marker": null
        },
        "content": [
         {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "-    Ketoconazole: ⍉1st-line oral agent d/t risk of drug-induced hepatitis"
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
         "indLeft": 36,
         "indRight": 0,
         "indFirst": -18,
         "spaceBefore": 0,
         "spaceAfter": 0,
         "line": {
          "rule": "auto",
          "value": 1
         },
         "align": "left",
         "shade": null,
         "borders": null,
         "marker": null
        },
        "content": [
         {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "-    Ketoconazole: ⇣cortisol in Cushing dz when ⍉surg candidate (w/ cabergoline, metyrapone)"
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
         "indLeft": 36,
         "indRight": 0,
         "indFirst": -18,
         "spaceBefore": 0,
         "spaceAfter": 0,
         "line": {
          "rule": "auto",
          "value": 1
         },
         "align": "left",
         "shade": null,
         "borders": null,
         "marker": null
        },
        "content": [
         {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "-    Tinea capitis: topical tx ineffective → oral antifungal — griseofulvin (1st-line), terbinafine (alternative 1st-line), itraconazole (if 1st-line tx fail)"
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
         "indLeft": 0,
         "indRight": 0,
         "indFirst": 0,
         "spaceBefore": 0,
         "spaceAfter": 0,
         "line": null,
         "align": "left",
         "shade": null,
         "borders": null,
         "marker": null
        },
        "content": [
         {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "-    Candidal balanitis: PO fluconazole"
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    }
